libdjvu: search the included files once each for a page component and a shape dictionary

DjVuImage::get_info(), get_bg44(), get_bgpm(), get_fgjb(), get_fgpm() and
get_fgbc() look for a component in the file of the page and then, depth first,
in the files it includes. DjVuFile::get_fgjd() looks the same way for the
shape dictionary that a JB2 mask (Sjbz) needs. A shared file included through
several paths is searched once for each path, so a chain of shared files that
each include the next two costs a number of visits that grows like the
Fibonacci numbers, though each file is created and decoded only once: 40 such
files take 50 s to draw an empty page, and a page whose mask needs a
dictionary over 30 of them takes 8 s.

Search the graph as DjVuFile::find_ndir() and get_merged_anno() walk it, with
a map of the URLs already visited, so that each file is searched once. The
first file found in depth-first order is the one the recursive search found:
a file is skipped only when an earlier visit searched it and everything it
includes without finding what is looked for. get_fgjd() waits for the files
still decoding and searches again, as before; each such pass searches each
file once. It used to be woken, and search again, for every chunk decoded in
any file below the page: a mask without its dictionary over a chain of 60
such files of 2000 small chunks each took 8 s to fail, where the same chain
decodes in 2.3 s without a mask. Only get_fgjd() waits on the chunk monitor
(wait_for_chunk()), and only a shape dictionary (Djbz) or a file that stops
decoding, which notify_file_flags_changed() still signals, can change what
it finds or whether it waits, so notify_chunk_done() wakes it for a Djbz
chunk alone. get_info() calls init_rotate() on the information it finds, as
before; its second call on the caller's own (empty) information is gone,
which never ran, as the first call leaves rotate_count at an orientation from
0 to 3.

The other walks over the included files that ddjvu reaches when it draws a
page already search each file once or do not recurse:
 - DjVuFile::get_merged_anno() (the annotations of a page, through
   DjVuImage::get_anno() and DjVuFile::merge_anno()), find_ndir() and
   decode_ndir() keep the same map;
 - DjVuPortcaster::compute_closure() (every notification between files)
   keeps a set of the ports it reached;
 - DjVuFile::get_anno(), get_text() and get_meta() read the file alone, and
   wait_for_finish(), decode_func(), notify_file_flags_changed(),
   trigger_cb() and process_incl_chunk() look at the files it includes
   directly.
DjVuFile::stop_decode() and stop() recurse once per path with no map, but only
when a document stops its files: ~DjVuDocument(), stop_init(),
check_unnamed_files() after a failed initialisation, and the child of a
stopped file. ddjvu entered neither while it drew a page over a chain of 20
such files, and it leaves through exit() when a page fails. DjVuDocEditor
walks the files for the editing commands of djvused, and
add_file_to_djvm() and local_get_url_names() of DjVuDocument, which keep a
map, for saving a document.

